# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`. On the Hugging Face Space the build context is
# the Space repo, which never contains .env (it is gitignored and the deploy
# script uses `git add -A`, which honours that). This file guards LOCAL
# `docker build` runs, where the context is your real working tree — without it,
# your live FMP / Databento / Anthropic / HF keys get baked into an image layer
# and survive even if a later layer deletes them.

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
.netrc

# VCS / build metadata. Nothing at runtime reads git — the Streamlit app loads
# only the parquet/db artifacts under data/processed.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Heavy caches the viewer does not read. All are gitignored, so they are absent
# from the Space context but present locally; excluding them keeps a local build
# from shipping several GB into the daemon.
data/raw/
data/processed/models/
data/processed/archive_*/
logs/
